+1 on this. Would also love a way to disable thinking at the model level in opencode.json, not just per-command.

I'm running qwen3.5:27b locally via Ollama and thinking mode adds massive overhead (27s vs <1s for simple queries). The native Ollama API supports "think": false but there's no way to pass that through OpenCode's OpenAI-compatible /v1 integration.

Something like this in the provider config would be ideal:

{
  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Ollama",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen3.5:27b": {
          "name": "qwen3.5:27b",
          "thinking": false
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

This would be especially useful for local models on consumer GPUs where thinking tokens eat into limited VRAM and slow everything down significantly.

This is my opencode.json configuration. I want to use a local model from Ollama, but tool calls don't work when I try to use it, even though the model itself supports tool usage. I've also increased the model's num_ctxparameter.

